00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:48.000
Karen's husband hired a team of three people. In desperation, Karen's husband turned to her. She was interested in the natural world, as a little girl she learned the Latin name of every butterfly in her neighborhood. While studying at Cornell, she'd taken all the courses the school offered in natural history. And tomology for insects or mythology for birds, paleontology for fossils, geology for rocks. But marine biology wasn't high on the list. So I said no, I really couldn't do that. I have three little children. I didn't want to go to work for my husband. He had enough to do, and I think that would
但他还是说服我至少读读那本手册。而那本手册及其蕴含的理念，在Karen心中点燃了火花。我必须试一试。Karen在手册中看到的是一种在过去几十年里在心理学界引发巨大争论的行为理论。它的影响深远，尤其是在教育领域。让我们花点时间回顾一下那段历史。在20世纪初，关于人们为何会有某种行为的一种主流观点来自西格蒙德·弗洛伊德。

